Z||000002||Haze_Performance||12-29-2000||04:24 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Robert:<BR><B>A customer of mine came in the shop the other day and clamed to know all about the Fiero.  He wondered why mine parked in front wasn’t burned up yet.  I asked him where he got all his information and he produced this magazine article.  What do you think?<BR>This is from the October 2000 issue.  <BR>Letters to the editor can be sent to: letters@automobilemag.com <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I get pissed every time I read that!!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003585.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003585.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">     <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 12-29-2000).]||||reg||13
Z||000003||2M4 Dale||12-29-2000||04:36 PM||||I wrote them this letter :<P>	After reading the very negative article about the Pontiac Fiero in your magazine I have come to the conclusion that you know very little about these automobiles. My Pontiac Fiero has 108,000 miles on it and is going strong. The idea that there is something wrong with these GREAT cars is nothing more than media hype. <BR>	My Fiero is stock and will outcorner anything,  American made, out there except for possibly the Corvette. Lets see...how much does a new VETTE cost ?...gee it seems that for about $3000 or less I can buy a 12-16 year old car that can compete with a Vette at any AutoX.    hmmmmmmm    It's true that my little 2.5L four cylinder is underpowered but the fact that my little car gets 34mpg+ has got to say something for the marque. <BR>	The reason GM killed the Fiero was purely due to the fact that the Fiero was tilling into Corvette sales. Now if you want to talk about a piece of crap...how about ANY of the C4 Vettes. I would rather have a Fiero ! No one at GM, Chevrolet, or Pontiac will own up to this however.<BR>	Now lets talk about Pontiacs/GMs  mistakes....killing the GTO....killing the Fiero....killing the F-body........building the AZTEC ?????? Go figure.<BR>	How about coming to the Fiero Festival in Williamsburg, Va. next summer and see what I'm talking about. I just bet that we (Fiero Fanatics) can show you the light.<P>                                                              Proud Fiero Owner, Dale L Starcher<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroowners.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroowners.com/</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.pennock.nl/forum.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pennock.nl/forum.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||12-29-2000||05:02 PM||||I've never seen the top one before.  This guy must be retarded or something.  If he writes his articles purely on his personal experiences and "hear-say", he shouldn't be a writer.  People aren't supposed to do that.  Sure, they can give their personal opinion, but they are supposed to give the subject the benefit of the doubt.  And he's telling us to get a life.  I don't know what "get a car" means, but I'm sure it's stupid.  Maybe we like our cars.  Just because he's probably driving around in a new Mercedes or SUV, it doesn't mean that older cars are necessarily bad.  That's a good letter that Dale sent.  I don't know why he didn't include those kind in his response.  He just was trying to get his point across.  He wanted to show other people that Fiero owners are psycho.  What a bastard.  I sent them an e-mail as well, but I wasn't as nice about it.  He deserved it though.  I'm sure he won't write anymore about Fieros.  Even if he does, we'll be waiting for him. <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||12-29-2000||05:05 PM||||Yeah, that editorial is pure garbage.  I still think its a tribute to the car to have any article like that in a magazine of that type.  They generally only write about new model cars, or super vintage/classics, but rarely anything in between.  Now if they would only get a good condition Fiero and actually drive it before just writing about them.  Oh well, at least Motor Trend gave the Fiero props when it wrote on the Opel Speedster recently.  The writer (was it Walton?) wants them to bring it to our shores and badge it a Fiero.  Finally someone who is writing favorable stuff about the Fiero!||||reg||1
